Project-specific context for the mock3 project:

Two codelines are in scope, both ESM TypeScript projects using vitest:
- mock-a at /home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-a — fare logic. Source lives in src/fares.ts, tests in test/fares.test.ts. Test command: `vitest run`. Type-check command: `tsc --noEmit`. No lint configured.
- mock-b at /home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-b — departure board / schedule rendering. Source lives in src/schedule.ts, tests in test/schedule.test.ts. Test command: `vitest run`. Type-check command: `tsc --noEmit`. No lint configured.

Tickets in scope:
- MOCK3-1: Riders aged exactly 65 are charged the adult fare. The bug is in `fareFor` in mock-a/src/fares.ts: the senior boundary check uses `rider.age > 65` instead of `rider.age >= 65`, so a rider aged exactly 65 falls through to BASE_FARE_CENTS (350) rather than CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS (175). When validating, confirm the injected diff changes the comparison to `>= 65` and that the test oracle includes a case for age exactly 65 expecting the concession fare.
- MOCK3-2: The departure board omits the final stop. The bug is in `formatStops` in mock-b/src/schedule.ts: the loop condition `i < stops.length - 1` skips the last element, so the final stop never appears in the output string. When validating, confirm the injected diff changes the loop bound so all stops are included (e.g. `i < stops.length`) and that the test oracle asserts the last stop name appears in the formatted output.

When classifying criteria, note that both projects use vitest with `describe`/`it`/`expect` from the `vitest` import. A passing test run in the injected evidence should show vitest output. If the injected evidence does not include a test run log, mark test-related criteria as untestable rather than assuming they pass.
